Anna —

We own the water. The bargemen cheered us, then immediately raised their prices, which is how you know things are returning to normal.

But I have darker news, and you should hear it from me before rumor improves it. The Duke has stopped pretending this is politics. His recruiters came back from the border hills with goblins. Paid in silver and pointed at farms. There is a word for a man who hires the wilderness against his own people, and the word is not Protector.

Harrowfield Manor is the proof. Lady Harrow declared for the old king's line a fortnight ago; three nights later her manor was burning and her people were barricaded in the stone hall, watching torches come up the road. Her rider reached us half-dead, and their message was four words: THEY ARE STILL COMING.

The Watch rides tonight. We cannot carry the fight to them — not with the numbers coming up that road. What we can do is stand in that hall and make the doorway more expensive than the Duke's silver.

Aldric said, "Ten turns of the glass until the Home Companies reach us. We hold ten." Wren checked her quiver and said nothing, which from Wren means yes.

The manor walls are cracked but the hall is good stone, and good stone forgives many sins. Hold the strong ground, sister. Let them come to us for once.

If the Companies are late, tell them I said something heroic.

— Elin
